  "notes": {
    "colorUsage": "Orange = primary action and emphasis ONLY. Navy = ink (headings, body-strong, icons) — never large navy fills; one full-navy surface per app for a single moment of gravitas. Olive/teal/plum do the supporting and decorative color work so orange does not flood the UI. No gradients: flat paper, white, and soft tints only.",
    "focus": "Inputs focus to a teal border plus a soft teal ring (ringFocus). Selected/active states are orange.",
    "press": "Primary buttons depress 1pt on press and drop their shadow. Cards lift 2pt on press-in where interactive. No bounces, no infinite decorative loops."
  },
  "domainNote": "All four domains share ONE color (olive-600 on olive-50, olive-700 ink). This is deliberate and load-bearing: a color never denotes a domain, and giving each domain its own hue invites exactly that reading. Domains are told apart by their glyph and name. Orange (action) and navy (ink) are deliberately not used here.",
